{{!--
Content of the « ••• » menu of the header (the earlier theme's submenu, in the new design): the most
recent posts as small cards with their date, then, below them, the most used public tags as a row of
plain bold links with « Tous les tags ». Rendered by header-body.hbs twice from the same data (the two
{{#get}} of header.hbs, no request from the browser): in the desktop popover (#site-discover: six posts,
one row on wide screens) and in the phone menu sheet (the first four posts as a list).
Parameters:
  prefix="..."   prefix of the ids of the headings (each use needs its own)
  count="6"      number of recent posts shown
  rowSizes="..."  sizes attribute of the posts' pictures: the width of their box (default: a compact row's, see row-item.hbs)
  posts          the recent posts ({{#get "posts"}} of header.hbs)
  tags           the most used public tags, with count.posts ({{#get "tags"}} of header.hbs)
--}}
<section class="discover__section discover__section--posts" aria-labelledby="{{prefix}}-recent">
  <h2 class="discover__title" id="{{prefix}}-recent">{{t "Recent posts"}}</h2>
  {{#if posts}}
    <ul class="discover__posts" role="list">
      {{#foreach posts limit=count}}<li>{{> row-item meta="tag-date" sizes=../rowSizes}}</li>{{/foreach}}
    </ul>
  {{/if}}
</section>
<section class="discover__section discover__section--tags" aria-labelledby="{{prefix}}-tags">
  <div class="discover__head">
    <h2 class="discover__title" id="{{prefix}}-tags">{{t "Tags"}}</h2>
    <a class="discover__all" href="{{@site.url}}/tags/">{{t "All tags"}}{{> "icons/arrow-right" class="icon-flip-rtl"}}</a>
  </div>
  {{#match tags.0.count.posts ">" 0}}
    <ul class="discover__tags" role="list">
      {{#foreach tags}}{{#match count.posts ">" 0}}<li><a class="discover__tag" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a></li>{{/match}}{{/foreach}}
    </ul>
  {{/match}}
</section>
